          "postId": "gsm-20261127090050-9a82f645-13da12b1e0a2",
          "sourcePath": "environment/sources-daily-opinions.md",
          "sample": {
            "id": "sample-d15476e1021b",
            "title": "讨论 2",
            "text": "### 讨论 2\n\n父回复关系未提供。\n\n1. **发言者 1**：I keep one adult crested gecko in a glass enclosure that I've had since he was small, and I'm starting to think about moving him into something taller. My current setup works, but it feels cramped when I add more climbing branches and foliage. I came across this REPTI ZOO RK0124N 24x18x36 Tall Glass Terrarium Review while browsing online: REPTI ZOO RK0124N 24x18x36 Tall Glass Terrarium Review. The dimensions sound like a good fit for a crested gecko, but I'm unsure about ventilation and whether the mesh top holds humidity well enough in a Maryland apartment that gets dry in winter. I also wonder if a single gecko would use all that vertical space or just stay near the top. Has anyone kept a crested gecko in a tall 24x18x36 glass tank? I'd like to hear how it holds heat and humidity before I decide.\n\n2. **发言者 2**：I have a single crested gecko in an 18\"x18\"x36\" enclosure and it does fine.  \n     \n   Aliza",
            "context": "采集时间：2026-11-27 13:21:13（北京时间）"
          }
        }
      ],
